Embracing each other, you all finally give way to tears. It appears, that by miracle you managed to avoid certain death. At last, you pull yourself together.
"Ok, we defeated him, aren't we?" you say, trying to make voice sound confident, "Conan, you did good! What would we do without you!"
It is hard to tell in the darkness, but it seems Conan blushed and tried to smile. You pull a blanket out of the rucksack.
"Let's try to sleep now. In the morning we'll decide what to do next."
You don't have to say it twice; in a minute everybody sleeps like a dog.